    "https://careers.cqu.edu.au/job/Rockhampton-Professor-Nursing-QLD/1331553566/": {
      "title": "Professor",
      "description": "Professor - Nursing Job Details | Central Queensland University Skip to main content Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Search by Location Show More Options Loading... Location All Department All State All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Professor - Nursing Posting Date: 8 Sept 2026 Type of Position: Continuing Location: Rockhampton, QLD, AU Cairns, QLD, AU Mackay, QLD, AU Townsville, QLD, AU About this Opportunity Continuing, Full-Time School of Nursing, Midwifery and Social Sciences CQUniversity Cairns, Mackay, Townsville or Rockhampton (other locations are negotiable, excl. SEQ region) (Relocation support available) Academic Level E: Total Remuneration $247,655 pa (including salary of $209,272 plus 17% superannuation and leave loading) Join an organisation with an unbreakable belief that quality education, training and research should be available to everyone – regardless of background, location or life circumstances. Working at CQUniversity CQUniversity is one of Australia's most inclusive and engaged universities, recognised for accessible education, impactful research and strong industry partnerships. The School of Nursing, Midwifery and Social Sciences is a leader in preparing healthcare professionals who make a meaningful difference across regional, rural and metropolitan communities. As a Professor in Nursing, you will provide exceptional academic leadership, driving excellence in teaching, research and industry engagement while shaping the strategic direction of nursing education and scholarship. You will lead multidisciplinary research initiatives, foster national and international collaborations, secure competitive research funding and contribute to the development of research and academic policy. Working closely with colleagues, students and external stakeholders, you will mentor and develop academic staff, supervise higher degree by research candidates, and champion innovative, evidence-based learning experiences. We are seeking an internationally recognised nursing scholar and academic leader with a distinguished record of research excellence, competitive funding success and strategic influence. You will bring the capability to shape the future direction of nursing education and research while enhancing CQUniversity's reputation nationally and globally. Be Rewarded 17% superannuation (with the choice to join an award-winning superfund) 5.4 weeks annual leave (plus 3 working days paid at Christmas and New Year closure) 10 days personal/sick leave, plus 5 days carer’s leave 7.25 hours engaged service leave Fantastic professional and career development opportunities Up to 26 weeks (six months) paid parental leave Access to an Employee Assistance Program and Fitness Passport Position Requirements Doctoral qualification (PhD or equivalent) plus significant experience in nursing. Current registration as a Registered Nurse (Division 1) with AHPRA and evidence of meeting NMBA Recency of Practice requirements. Extensive academic, research and industry experience, with a distinguished record of achievement in nursing education and scholarship. Demonstrated success in leading high-performing multidisciplinary teams, mentoring academic staff and driving strategic teaching and research outcomes. Distinguished research profile, evidenced by high-quality publications, successful supervision of Higher Degree by Research candidates and a strong record of competitive research funding success. Established national and international standing in the profession, demonstrated through leadership, research collaboration and engagement with professional bodies and key stakeholders. Proven ability to influence the direction of nursing education, research and professional practice through strategic partnerships with industry, government and the broader community. Pre-Employment Checks Appointment to this role is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks, which may include a National Police Check and/or Working with Children Check (where applicable). The University is committed to providing a safe, inclusive and respectful environment where its members can study, work and live free from gender-based violence. In line with our organisational values and regulatory obligations, applicants may be required to declare any past or current allegations, investigations or findings relating to gender-based violence. The successful candidate may also be required to demonstrate that they meet the “fit and proper person” criteria as required under applicable legislation and regulatory frameworks (including ASQA requirements where relevant). Our Commitment to Inclusion At CQUniversity, inclusivity is at the heart of who we are. We are committed to creating a workplace where everyone feels respected, supported and empowered to succeed regardless of background or ability. We advance reconciliation through our Stretch Reconciliation Action Plan (RAP), First Nations Workforce Strategy and our First Nations Cultural Competency Framework , strengthening opportunities for First Nations peoples and embedding cultural respect across our organisation. Through our Disability-Informed Action Plan, we continue to enhance accessibility and inclusion across our University. As a recognised member of the Hidden Disabilities Sunflower Program , we actively promote awareness and understanding of non-visible disabilities, helping to ensure everyone can bring their whole selves to work and thrive. CQUniversity is also committed to providing an accessible, equitable and inclusive recruitment and selection process. The University will provide reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment, selection, appointment and onboarding process to ensure people with disability can participate on an equal basis with others. Position Description For further information about this position, please refer to the Position Description . Apply today for a career that changes lives Applications Close: 11:59pm, Wednesday, 7 October 2026 Job Requisition ID: 6819 Contact Details: Lisa Wirihana (07) 4930 9015 l.wirihana@cqu.edu.au When submitting your application, please include: Your Current CV or Resume, and a 1-2 page Cover Letter highlighting your relevant skills, experience and suitability for the position. Work Rights: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold the full rights to work in Australia to be considered for this appointment. CQUniversity is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes diversity in the workplace. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and CQUniversity’s domestic and international student graduates with post-study work rights are encouraged to apply. #ACADE || #LI-JF1 || #LI-Onsite || Keywords: Academic Leadership | Teaching and Learning Higher Education | Nursing Education | Social Sciences | Nursing Education Leadership | Healthcare Workforce Development | Nursing Workforce Strategy | Nursing Education Innovation | Leadership in Health Education | Curriculum Development |  Government Collaboration | Clinical Academic | Nurse Consultant | Credentialed Nurse | Translational Health | Clinical Leadership | Professional Practice Leadership | Clinical Scholar | Health Sector Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Jobs, Academic & ELICOS Jobs Disclaimer Accessibility Feedback Policy Privacy Right to Information Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CRICOS Provider Code: 00219C   RTO Code 40939   CQUniversity Australia is a trading name of Central Queensland University."
    },
    "https://careers.cqu.edu.au/job/Rockhampton-Associate-Professor-Nursing-QLD/1367016366/": {
      "title": "Associate Professor",
      "description": "Associate Professor - Nursing Job Details | Central Queensland University Skip to main content Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Search by Location Show More Options Loading... Location All Department All State All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Associate Professor - Nursing Posting Date: 8 Sept 2026 Type of Position: Continuing Location: Rockhampton, QLD, AU Townsville, QLD, AU Cairns, QLD, AU Mackay, QLD, AU About this Opportunity Continuing, Full-Time School of Nursing, Midwifery and Social Sciences CQUniversity Cairns, Mackay, Townsville or Rockhampton (other locations are negotiable, excl. SEQ region) Relocation support available Academic Level D: Total Remuneration $196,588 to $214,609 pa (including salary of $166,120 to $181,348 plus 17% superannuation and leave loading) Join an organisation with an unbreakable belief that quality education, training and research should be available to everyone – regardless of background, location or life circumstances. Working at CQUniversity CQUniversity is one of Australia's most inclusive and engaged universities, renowned for its commitment to accessible education, impactful research and strong industry partnerships. The School of Nursing, Midwifery and Social Sciences is a leader in preparing healthcare professionals who make a meaningful difference across regional, rural and metropolitan communities. As an Associate Professor in Nursing, you will provide significant academic leadership within the School, contributing to the strategic direction and ongoing success of nursing education and research. This is an exciting opportunity for an accomplished academic to influence the future of the discipline through innovative teaching, impactful research, industry engagement and the mentorship of emerging academics and researchers. You will lead and contribute to the delivery of contemporary nursing curriculum, coordinate courses, supervise higher degree by research candidates, and foster collaborative partnerships with healthcare providers, professional bodies and community stakeholders. Your expertise will play a vital role in advancing student success, strengthening research capability and enhancing CQU's reputation for excellence in nursing education. We are seeking a respected academic leader with a strong track record in teaching and learning, research performance and external engagement, who can contribute to the continued growth of nursing education and research at CQUniversity. Be Rewarded 17% superannuation (with the choice to join an award-winning superfund) 5.4 weeks annual leave (plus 3 working days paid at Christmas and New Year closure) 10 days personal/sick leave, plus 5 days carer’s leave 7.25 hours engaged service leave Fantastic professional and career development opportunities Up to 26 weeks (six months) paid parental leave Access to an Employee Assistance Program and Fitness Passport Position Requirements Doctoral qualification (PhD or equivalent) plus significant experience in nursing. Current registration as a Registered Nurse (Division 1) with AHPRA. Demonstrated excellence in teaching, supervision and curriculum development across undergraduate and postgraduate nursing education. Established research profile, including publication in high-quality journals and success in securing competitive research funding. Proven leadership capability in research, teaching and/or academic governance, with a commitment to mentoring colleagues and fostering a positive team culture. Strong industry and community engagement, with the ability to develop and maintain effective professional partnerships and networks. Internationally recognised contributions to the discipline and a demonstrated commitment to advancing the nursing profession. Pre-Employment Checks Appointment to this role is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks, which may include a National Police Check and/or Working with Children Check (where applicable). The University is committed to providing a safe, inclusive and respectful environment where its members can study, work and live free from gender-based violence. In line with our organisational values and regulatory obligations, applicants may be required to declare any past or current allegations, investigations or findings relating to gender-based violence. The successful candidate may also be required to demonstrate that they meet the “fit and proper person” criteria as required under applicable legislation and regulatory frameworks (including ASQA requirements where relevant). Our Commitment to Inclusion At CQUniversity, inclusivity is at the heart of who we are. We are committed to creating a workplace where everyone feels respected, supported and empowered to succeed regardless of background or ability. We advance reconciliation through our Stretch Reconciliation Action Plan (RAP), First Nations Workforce Strategy and our First Nations Cultural Competency Framework , strengthening opportunities for First Nations peoples and embedding cultural respect across our organisation. Through our Disability-Informed Action Plan, we continue to enhance accessibility and inclusion across our University. As a recognised member of the Hidden Disabilities Sunflower Program , we actively promote awareness and understanding of non-visible disabilities, helping to ensure everyone can bring their whole selves to work and thrive. CQUniversity is also committed to providing an accessible, equitable and inclusive recruitment and selection process. The University will provide reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment, selection, appointment and onboarding process to ensure people with disability can participate on an equal basis with others. Position Description For further information about this position, please refer to the Position Description . Apply today for a career that changes lives Applications Close: 11:59pm, Wednesday, 7 October 2026 Job Requisition ID: 7605 Contact Details: Lisa Wirihana (07) 4930 9015 l.wirihana@cqu.edu.au When submitting your application, please include: Your Current CV or Resume, and a 1-2 page Cover Letter highlighting your relevant skills, experience and suitability for the position. Work Rights: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold the full rights to work in Australia to be considered for this appointment. CQUniversity is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes diversity in the workplace. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and CQUniversity’s domestic and international student graduates with post-study work rights are encouraged to apply. #ACADD || #LI-JF1 || #LI-Onsite || Keywords: Academic Leadership | Teaching and Learning Higher Education | Nursing Education | Social Sciences | Nursing Education Leadership | Healthcare Workforce Development | Nursing Workforce Strategy | Nursing Education Innovation | Leadership in Health Education | Curriculum Development | Government Collaboration | Clinical Academic | Nurse Consultant | Credentialed Nurse | Translational Health | Clinical Leadership | Professional Practice Leadership | Clinical Scholar | Health Sector Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Jobs, Academic & ELICOS Jobs Disclaimer Accessibility Feedback Policy Privacy Right to Information Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CRICOS Provider Code: 00219C   RTO Code 40939   CQUniversity Australia is a trading name of Central Queensland University."
